import pathlib,json,html
J=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent
L=lambda p:json.loads(p.read_text())
d=L(J/'receipts/topfive-diff.json');e=L(J/'receipts/topfive-extended.json')
rows=[dict(variant='site share',scope=r['view'],caps='see metric',**r) for r in d['rows']]+e['rows']
inputs={k:d['v17-share'] for k,d in L(J/'src/inputs.json').items()}
summary=''.join('<tr><td>'+html.escape(s['display'])+'</td>'+''.join('<td>'+f'{s[f]:.3f}'+'</td>' for f in ['capability'])+''.join('<td>'+f'{s["axes"][f]:.3f}'+'</td>' for f in ['speed','cost'])+'<td>'+html.escape(s['listing'])+'</td></tr>' for s in inputs.values())
text='''<!doctype html><meta charset="utf-8"><title>JevBench v1.7.2 candidate</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1400px;margin:32px auto;background:#101723;color:#e4edf8;padding:20px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #344258;text-align:left}input,select{padding:8px;margin:12px;background:#25344a;color:white}small{color:#a3b8d3}.changed{background:#633}</style><h1>JevBench v1.7.1 → v1.7.2</h1><p>Complete aggregate candidate preview. Raw hash verified in place; frozen category and decisive extraction completed. Release review remains PENDING. One same-draw addition; no method change. All 288 carried rows retain scores and confidence intervals; placements alone move. No measurement or scoring repeated.</p><p>40 site-assembled top-five lists: <b>0 changes</b>. Supplementary off/share comparison: <b>EXTENDED</b>. No lists change.</p><table><thead><tr><th>New model<th>Capability<th>Speed<th>Cost axis<th>Treatment</tr></thead><tbody>SUMMARY</tbody></table><p><small>Jeetu Decider 2B is within the official cost cap. Off comparisons reuse preserved v1.6 values and pinned original off outputs for the 26 v1.7.0-new, four GPU remeasured and three v1.7.1-new rows; no values are invented. The share comparison uses the site assembly against the complete v1.7.2 candidate in an isolated synthetic review tree; the actual manifest remains PENDING. This local aggregate preview grants no publication authority.</small></p><input id="query" placeholder="Filter scope, variant or metric"><label><input type="checkbox" id="only">Changed only</label><span id="count"></span><table><thead><tr><th>Variant / scope / caps<th>Metric<th>Before top five<th>After top five<th>Changed</tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table><script>const data=DATA;function render(){const q=document.querySelector('#query').value.toLowerCase(),only=document.querySelector('#only').checked;const rows=data.filter(r=>(!only||r.changed)&&[r.variant,r.scope,r.caps,r.metric].join(' ').toLowerCase().includes(q));document.querySelector('#count').textContent=rows.length+' lists';document.querySelector('#rows').innerHTML=rows.map(r=>`<tr class="${r.changed?'changed':''}"><td>${r.variant} / ${r.scope} / ${r.caps}</td><td>${r.metric}</td><td>${r.before.join('<br>')}</td><td>${r.after.join('<br>')}</td><td>${r.changed?'YES':'No'}</td></tr>`).join('')}document.querySelector('#query').oninput=render;document.querySelector('#only').onchange=render;render()</script>'''
text=text.replace('EXTENDED',f"{e['changed_lists']} of {e['lists']} changed").replace('SUMMARY',summary).replace('DATA',json.dumps(rows))
(J/'preview').mkdir(exist_ok=True);(J/'preview/index.html').write_text(text)
print('Preview:',J/'preview/index.html')
